subproblem.statement:
Let P, d ∈ ℕ, O ⊆ ℝ^P open, x ∈ O, g : ℝ^P → ℝ^d, ψ : ℝ^d → ℝ^P, Q : ℝ^d → L(ℝ^P, ℝ^P) and a, b ∈ ℝ; put v := g(x). Assume:
- g is differentiable at x, and ψ and Q are differentiable at v;
- Q(g(z))(z − ψ(g(z))) = 0 for all z ∈ O;
- Q(v)∘Dψ(v) = Dψ(v) and ‖Q(v)‖ ≤ 1;
- a ≥ 0, b ≥ 0 and ‖DQ(v)‖ ≤ a;
- |w| ≤ b|Dψ(v)w| for all w ∈ ℝ^d;
- ab|x − ψ(v)| ≤ 1/2.
Then ‖D(ψ∘g)(x)‖ ≤ 1 + 2ab|x − ψ(v)| (operator norm).
